From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:30:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: firmware: google,gs101-acpm-ipc: add the thermal
 sensors

On gs101 the TMU belongs to the APM, and the kernel reads temperatures
by asking the ACPM firmware over its TMU channel. Describe that as a
thermal-sensor child of the ACPM node, as the PMICs are.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 .../firmware/google,gs101-acpm-ipc.yaml       | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/google,gs101-acpm-ipc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/google,gs101-acpm-ipc.yaml
index 3594fb906..7005da5ea 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/google,gs101-acpm-ipc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/firmware/google,gs101-acpm-ipc.yaml
@@ -73,6 +73,25 @@ properties:
     type: object
     additionalProperties: true
 
+  thermal-sensor:
+    description:
+      The SoC's thermal sensors, which the ACPM firmware reads on the
+      kernel's behalf. Cells are the sensor index (0 big, 1 mid, 2 little
+      CPU cluster, 3 GPU, 4 ISP, 5 TPU).
+    type: object
+    $ref: /schemas/thermal/thermal-sensor.yaml#
+    unevaluatedProperties: false
+
+    properties:
+      compatible:
+        const: google,gs101-acpm-tmu
+
+      "#thermal-sensor-cells":
+        const: 1
+
+    required:
+      - compatible
+
   shmem:
     description:
       List of phandle pointing to the shared memory (SHM) area. The memory
